#### 3.1.2 Algorithm Design

Algorithm [1](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.12087v3#alg1 "Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.1.2 Algorithm Design ‣ 3.1 Pruning Attention with Running Maximums ‣ 3 Methodology") presents our modified FlashAttention forward pass. The key modification is the introduction of a dynamic pruning condition that saves both computation and memory bandwidth. Where We Save: When m~i(j)−mi(j)<ln⁡(λ)\tilde{m}\_{i}^{(j)}-m\_{i}^{(j)}<\ln(\lambda) (line 7), we skip:

